## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses practical expertise in building production ML systems at the edge. It tests understanding of latency-constrained deployment, multilingual model design, safety-critical systems, and operational robustness. Candidates must demonstrate knowledge of model compression techniques (quantization, distillation), architectural patterns (cascaded models), evaluation methodology, and deployment strategies with fallback mechanisms.

## Key Concepts

- Edge deployment with quantization and distillation
- Cascaded model architecture for efficiency
- Safety policy alignment and classifier training
- Multilingual evaluation with per-language metrics
- Drift detection and automated rollback

## Implementation Approach

```javascript
async function processMessage(message, context) {
  const start = Date.now();

  // Step 1: Safety check (blocking - prioritize safety over latency)
  const safetyResult = await context.safety.classify(message);
  if (!safetyResult.safe) {
    return { response: context.templates.safetyFallback(), latency: Date.now() - start };
  }

  // Step 2: Intent detection (on-device transformer)
  const intent = await context.intent.detect(message, { language: message.lang });

  // Step 3: Check latency budget before server escalation
  const elapsed = Date.now() - start;
  if (elapsed > 400 && intent.requiresServer) {
    return await context.server.escalate(message, intent);
  }

  // Step 4: Generate response
  return { 
    response: context.response.generate(intent, message), 
    latency: Date.now() - start 
  };
}
```
